  "title": "The One Due Diligence Mistake That Could Tank Your Business Acquisition",
  "date": "2025-04-11T17:06:59.958Z",
  "content": {
    "text": "96\n\n The One Due Diligence Mistake That Could Tank Your Business Acquisition\nHi Sara,\nBuying a business? You\u2019re probably knee-deep in financial statements, debt service coverage ratios, and making sure the numbers check out.\nBut do you know what most buyers completely ignore?\nThe employee handbook.\nYes, that legally questionable 70-page document no one\u2014including the seller\u2014has ever actually read. And yet, skipping it nearly torpedoed a deal I worked on last week.\nThe Landmine Hiding in Plain Sight\nA buyer was acquiring a small business\u2014just five employees, all women. Everyone was excited. I casually asked for the employment handbook, mostly as a formality.\nThey sent it over as a joke, like, \u201cSure, if you really want to waste your time.\u201d\nWell, guess what I found?\nThe seller had unknowingly adopted big-company policies (think FMLA, ADA) that didn\u2019t even apply to them.\nBuried in the fine print? A 12-week paid maternity leave policy\u2014which the seller had no idea existed.\nThe five employees? They definitely knew.\nNow the buyer had a tough choice:\n\u279d Match the policy and take a financial hit.\n\u279d Cut it and risk losing the entire team post-close.\nOh, and they weren\u2019t allowed to talk to employees before closing\u2014so they had to make the call blind.\nWhy This Matters (Even in an Asset Purchase)\n\"It\u2019s an asset purchase\u2014I\u2019m not taking on liabilities, so who cares?\"\nBecause you\u2019re not just buying assets, you\u2019re buying people. Employees don\u2019t magically reset their expectations just because ownership changes hands.\nIf you don\u2019t honor policies they were promised, they\u2019ll leave.\nWhat You Should Be Checking (That You\u2019re Probably Not)\n\u279d The employee handbook (yes, really\u2014just skim it).\n \u279d Hidden liabilities in PTO, benefits, or outdated workplace policies that could become your problem.\n \u279d Anything that might make employees feel like they got a raw deal when you take over.\nMost buyers only realize this after key employees start quitting\u2014or when they find themselves stuck with unexpected financial obligations.\nDon\u2019t be that buyer.\nIf you want to avoid post-close chaos, check out our courses on Deal Academy for expert guidance on running a smooth diligence process.\nTo deals that don\u2019t implode,\nSara Sharp\nPartner, SK&S Law Group\nBusiness Consultant & Founder of Deal Academy\nP.S. If you're looking to buy or sell an accounting firm, and want me to keep an eye out for you, fill out this form here.\n\n For more helpful lessons from Deal Academy, check out our Dealmakers Youtube Channel where you'll find Sara's Weekly Wine Down, where she talks about what she's seen in the industry this week and interviews with M&A Experts and Dealmakers.\nYou can check out some recent Dealmakers podcast episodes by clicking the images below.\n\n Copyright \u00a9 2025\u00a0 Someday Consultants, All rights reserved. \n\n Our e-mail address is:\ninfo@dealacademy.org\n\n Want to change how you receive these emails?\n You can unsubscribe from this list.",
